PREFIX: ZEF-IMP
ROOT: False
OPTIONS:
  ENABLE_MID: False
  MARKUP: Text

[TEXT]
STATEMENT: >>>
IMPLEMENTATION items choose the concrete solution. The remaining work is to
write and verify the code at the linked paths. Each item has an INTERFACE parent
and a planned code link; a missing code file means planned, not unlinked.
<<<

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Build, configuration, and common failure handling

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ZEF-IMP-001
TITLE: Configuration header and assertions
STATEMENT: Add the compile-time configuration header, exact-width public types, range checks, layout checks, and configuration-test fixtures.
COMMENT: Code link: framework/include/zef_config.h; tests/configuration/.
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: ZEF-IF-004

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ZEF-IMP-002
TITLE: Opaque public object headers
STATEMENT: Use forward-declared opaque runtime types and caller-owned storage handles in the public headers.
COMMENT: Code link: framework/include/zef_types.h; framework/include/zef_api.h.
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: ZEF-IF-001
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: ZEF-IF-003

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ZEF-IMP-003
TITLE: Panic and result implementation
STATEMENT: Implement the result enums, panic reasons, diagnostic payload, non-returning panic adapter, and host capture hook.
COMMENT: Code link: framework/core/zef_panic.c; framework/include/zef_panic.h; tests/panic/.
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: ZEF-IF-002

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Message, Mailbox, and Machine implementation

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ZEF-IMP-010
TITLE: Fixed message pools and envelope
STATEMENT: Use fixed aligned block pools with a bounded free-list, an opaque envelope, a building/sealed state bit, a topic, exact payload length, and an internal claim counter.
COMMENT: Code link: framework/core/zef_pool.c; framework/core/zef_message.c; framework/include/zef_message.h.
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: ZEF-IF-010
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: ZEF-IF-012

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ZEF-IMP-011
TITLE: Claim transfer and reclamation
STATEMENT: Implement normal post as claim transfer, shared post as retain-before-enqueue, dequeue transfer, publication claim accounting, checked release, and immediate final-release return to the originating pool.
COMMENT: Code link: framework/core/zef_message.c; tests/message_ownership/.
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: ZEF-IF-011

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ZEF-IMP-012
TITLE: Ring Mailbox
STATEMENT: Use a monotonic head/tail ring over caller-provided const Message pointers, with conditional wrap for arbitrary capacities, front insertion, statistics, and stable selective removal.
COMMENT: Code link: framework/core/zef_mailbox.c; framework/include/zef_mailbox.h.
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: ZEF-IF-013

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ZEF-IMP-020
TITLE: Descriptor-based Machine
STATEMENT: Represent each State node with immutable parent, initial, handler, enter, and leave fields; keep only the current node and startup state in the Machine; use bounded local traversal storage for transitions.
COMMENT: Code link: framework/core/zef_machine.c; framework/include/zef_machine.h.
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: ZEF-IF-020
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: ZEF-IF-021

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ZEF-IMP-030
TITLE: Reactor registry and cleanup
STATEMENT: Implement a zero-based registry with explicit lifecycle state, mailbox cleanup, runnable-bit cleanup, timer detach, subscription removal, and detectable repeated removal.
COMMENT: Code link: framework/core/zef_reactor.c; framework/include/zef_reactor.h.
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: ZEF-IF-022

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Kernel, topics, and time

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ZEF-IMP-040
TITLE: Cooperative Kernel bitmap
STATEMENT: Use one runnable bitmap indexed by zero-based Reactor identity, highest-set-bit selection, one-message run_one dispatch, and an idle callback in run_forever.
COMMENT: Code link: framework/core/zef_kernel.c; framework/include/zef_kernel.h.
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: ZEF-IF-030

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ZEF-IMP-050
TITLE: Bitmap topic table
STATEMENT: Use one subscriber bitmap per topic, snapshot it inside the port critical section, and deliver the shared sealed Message in priority order.
COMMENT: Code link: framework/core/zef_topics.c; framework/include/zef_topics.h.
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: ZEF-IF-031

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ZEF-IMP-060
TITLE: Delta-list Clock service
STATEMENT: Use a caller-owned delta list, explicit timer state, immediate unlink on stop, enqueue-only expiry handling, periodic reinsertion, and a documented same-tick rule.
COMMENT: Code link: framework/core/zef_clock.c; framework/include/zef_clock.h.
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: ZEF-IF-032

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Ports, optional preemption, and verification

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ZEF-IMP-070
TITLE: Host port
STATEMENT: Implement saved-state fake interrupt masking, nested restoration, reschedule observation, idle observation, and non-returning panic capture for host tests.
COMMENT: Code link: framework/ports/host/zef_port_host.c; tests/port_host/.
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: ZEF-IF-040

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ZEF-IMP-071
TITLE: Cortex-M0 port
STATEMENT: Map critical sections to PRIMASK, rescheduling to PendSV request, idle to the target low-power hook, and panic to the target safe-state policy; document kernel-aware interrupts.
COMMENT: Code link: framework/ports/cortex-m0/zef_port_cortex_m0.c; framework/ports/cortex-m0/zef_pendsv.S.
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: ZEF-IF-040

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ZEF-IMP-073
TITLE: Public API interrupt-context annotations
STATEMENT: Add an explicit ISR-safe, thread-only, or ISR-variant classification to every application-callable public API function and macro, including stated preconditions, boundedness limits, ownership rules, and fatal-error behavior; add ISR-specific operations where the classification requires them.
COMMENT: Code link: public headers and API documentation; ISR-context consumer tests.
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: ZEF-IF-041

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ZEF-IMP-072
TITLE: Optional PendSV scheduler
STATEMENT: Implement per-Reactor process stacks, valid exception frames, callee-saved register save and restore, highest-eligible-runnable selection, and safe removal of a terminated Reactor.
COMMENT: Code link: framework/ports/cortex-m0/zef_pendsv.S; framework/ports/cortex-m0/zef_context.c.
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: ZEF-IF-040

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ZEF-IMP-080
TITLE: Consumer and behavior test matrix
STATEMENT: Add public-header consumer tests, unit tests, property tests, integration tests, configuration variants, and sanitizer builds covering each WHAT and INTERFACE item before phase exit.
COMMENT: Code link: tests/; CMake test targets; source relation markers in implementation and test files.
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: ZEF-IF-050

[[/SECTION]]
